message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "rfm-pipeline: A Python package for reduced-form modeling pipelines"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hettinger
    given-names: Dylan
    email: dylan.hettinger@nlr.gov
    affiliation: National Renewable Energy Laboratory
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NatLabRockies/rfm-pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/NatLabRockies/rfm-pipeline"
abstract: >-
  rfm-pipeline is a Python package for fitting interpretable multi-output
  reduced-form models from prepared training and holdout tables. It provides
  regularized feature screening, output-wise linear fitting, holdout
  evaluation, and portable coefficient and metadata bundles.
